      <!-- callouts -->
      <g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="700">
        <g><circle cx="78" cy="125" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="78" y="129" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="300" cy="45" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="300" y="49" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="300" cy="97" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="300" y="101" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="300" cy="190" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="300" y="194" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Surface</strong> — the card vocabulary: <code>--fl-radius-card</code>,
          1px border, 24px padding. Flex column; long bodies scroll inside
          while title and actions stay pinned.</li>
      <li><strong>Title</strong> — the headline size (24px/400), wired with
          <code>aria-labelledby</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Body</strong> — supporting text, or a
          <a href="text-fields.html">field</a> for form dialogs.</li>
      <li><strong>Actions</strong> — right-aligned; Cancel as a text button,
          the confirm as filled — or <code>fl-btn--danger</code>
          (<code>--fl-error</code>) for destructive confirms.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Markup contract:</strong> any element with
        <code>data-fl-open="dialog-id"</code> opens it;
        <code>data-fl-close</code> inside the dialog closes it; or close it
        yourself with <code>flint.dialog.close(el)</code> /
        <code>el.close()</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancel/confirm results are free:</strong> put the actions in
        <code>&lt;form method="dialog"&gt;</code> — submitting closes the
        dialog and records the pressed button's <code>value</code> in
        <code>dialog.returnValue</code>. Read it after close; no extra JS.
        Buttons outside the form can still submit it with the
        <code>form</code> attribute.</li>
    <li><strong>Focus:</strong> moves to the first focusable control on open;
        returns to the invoker on every close path (button, Escape, scrim
        click, submit).</li>
    <li><strong>Dismissal:</strong> Escape and scrim clicks both close. If a
        dialog must not be dismissible (unsaved changes), that is an author
        decision: prevent the native <code>cancel</code> event and hide
        <code>data-fl-close</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Stacking:</strong> a dialog can open over a
        <a href="bottom-sheet.html">bottom sheet</a> (or another dialog) —
        the top layer stacks them in DOM order and Escape peels only the top
        one.</li>
    <li><strong>Scroll lock:</strong> the page locks while any overlay is
        open, restored on close.</li>
    <li><strong>Animation:</strong> 150ms fade + scale in, slide/scale out,
        scrim fading on the same clock — all CSS,
        <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> disables it entirely.</li>
    <li><strong>No-JS fallback (honest):</strong> without flint.js the dialog
        stays hidden and the page keeps working — the content is not lost,
        it just can't be opened. Call <code>showModal()</code> yourself with
        one line, or drive it from your own code; the CSS has no JS
        dependencies. See the <a href="overlay.html">overlay infra
        demo</a> for the raw lifecycle.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give the dialog <code>aria-labelledby</code> pointing at its title —
        the screen reader announces the dialog by name.</li>
    <li>The inert background is native: nothing behind the dialog is
        focusable, clickable or announced. No <code>aria-hidden</code> is
        juggled on the page — the classic bug doesn't exist here.</li>
    <li>Focus starts on the first control (usually Cancel — the safe choice)
        and cycles within the dialog. Keep Cancel first in the DOM.</li>
    <li><code>fl-btn--danger</code> uses <code>--fl-error</code> (#d93025,
        4.9:1 on white — AA for its 14px/500 text).</li>
    <li>Don't remove the focus ring; the global <code>:focus-visible</code>
        ring is what makes the trap visible to keyboard users.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

